# --- CUSTOM (radata fork): deployment tooling ---------------------------------
# THIS REPO IS PUBLIC (fork of NdoleStudio/httpsms). Nothing describing how or
# where we deploy belongs in it.
#
# ops/ is NOT tracked: the build and deploy scripts name the bastion host, the
# ssh port, the login user, the server paths and the release layout. They live
# only on disk and on the deploy host. Release tarballs under ops/tmp/ are also
# ~50MB each, which is reason enough on its own.
**/ops/
# files parked during the api/web split
*.superseded
# The real api dev stack: names the bastion host, ssh port, login user and the
# private key path. api/docker-compose.example.yml is the sanitised template
# that ships instead.
api/docker-compose.yml
# Our Firebase config: project id, app id, oauth client and the Android API
# key. Upstream TRACKS this file, so it was inherited tracked and .gitignore
# alone could never have held it back — it needed git rm --cached, which is
# why it reached GitHub twice. Keep it local; the build fails loudly without
# it and ops/build-release.sh already gates on it.
android/app/google-services.json

# Working notes — investigation write-ups, open questions, things parked for
# later. Local thinking, not documentation, and it names this deployment's hosts
# and Firebase project in passing. It reached a commit once (1d1757f, reset
# before it was pushed); this is what stops the next one.
__to_do/


